"""Incremental human-authored synthesis; references only reviewed bodies."""
import hashlib,json,pathlib
H=pathlib.Path(__file__).resolve().parent;P='additional_operad_skills_remaining';f=json.loads((H/(P+'_preparation.json')).read_text())['files'];rp=H/(P+'.json');r=json.loads(rp.read_text())
def e(i,a,b):
    x=f[i];return {'path':x['path'],'sha256':x['sha256'],'lines':[a,b]}
claims=[
{'id':'OPSKILL-C001','claim':'The shared corpus contains useful claim-hygiene procedures that explicitly distinguish declared structure, bounded diagnostics, proofs, replay custody and authority.','evidence':[e(2,1,228),e(9,55,176),e(15,31,96)],'dependencies':['A caller must load and follow the referenced contract; actual checker owners remain separate.'],'limitations':['This is a source-backed account of guidance, not evidence that agent workflows comply or improve accuracy.']},
{'id':'OPSKILL-C002','claim':'The historical-campaign design separates snapshot custody, base-sensitive computation, causal-edge support and independent recurrence; immutable proposed candidates cannot themselves mint admission.','evidence':[e(19,92,192),e(19,229,243),e(19,261,291)],'dependencies':['Complete raw captures, bound policies, actual controls and external admission would be needed for execution.'],'limitations':['The source explicitly says the 2,115-PR campaign is not completed. Three clusters is a nomination threshold, not a general statistical guarantee.']},
{'id':'OPSKILL-C003','claim':'Generated lesson packages offer reusable finite review components for denominators, input-work admission, complete typed answer bindings, premise transfer and task-matched guards while usually disclaiming ambient activation.','evidence':[e(38,19,60),e(48,19,80),e(50,19,67),e(56,19,100),e(58,19,63)],'dependencies':['Typed catalog ownership and source pins; original task schema, eligible benign baseline and independent deciding checker.'],'limitations':['Historical witness descriptions are not new replays. Six independent tiny controls check arithmetic/literal statements only; no retained skill execution or general detector accuracy is established.']},
{'id':'OPSKILL-C004','claim':'Templates provide organizational interfaces, but mathematical nouns do not by themselves establish functors, natural transformations, suboperads, evaluation algebras or convergence.','evidence':[e(4,26,93),e(26,18,51),e(27,18,55),e(30,35,55),e(35,18,43)],'dependencies':['Explicit objects/carriers, maps/actions, units/composition, closure and required law witnesses.'],'limitations':['The finding concerns what these templates establish; it does not deny separately implemented typed-tree checks in other source owners.']}
]
findings=[
{'id':'OPSKILL-F001','severity':'medium','title':'Live categorical templates conflate different mathematical structures','finding':'The live 2-morphism template calls an ordered sequence of skills a natural transformation eta:f=>g, without parallel functors, components or naturality. The capability template calls colour/license lists a suboperad and evaluation algebra without units/closure or actions. These are useful routing declarations but do not establish the named mathematical structures.','evidence':[e(35,18,43),e(27,18,55),e(26,34,38),e(4,85,93)],'recommended_action':'Label the legacy category templates as illustrative or retired and require explicit law-bearing owners before asserting categorical semantics. Keep syntactic signature checks distinct from mathematical construction.','validation':'Full source reading; definitional mismatch, not a runtime replay.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F002','severity':'medium','title':'Approval example admits an explicit negative decision','finding':'The unanchored grep for APPROVED also accepts NOT APPROVED and UNAPPROVED, so the shown gate does not enforce the claimed approval state or bind it to the current revision.','evidence':[e(8,70,81)],'recommended_action':'Read an exact typed decision field bound to the reviewed revision; reject missing/ambiguous state.','validation':'OPSKILL-CHECK-002 independently confirms the literal match. Git Bash could not initialize, so no actual grep execution is claimed.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F003','severity':'high','title':'Broken-link failures do not reach the compliance script exit flag','finding':'scan_links pipes output into a while loop whose bad() call changes fail in a pipeline subshell. Under normal Bash/POSIX pipeline execution, a link-only failure leaves outer fail=0 and the final script can print PASS and exit zero.','evidence':[e(10,8,16),e(10,86,108)],'recommended_action':'Run the loop in the parent shell or explicitly propagate its status; add an otherwise-valid broken-link negative fixture and assert nonzero exit.','validation':'Source-level control-flow finding. OPSKILL-CHECK-001 was NOT RUN: MSYS failed before the minimal isolated fragment with NtCreateDirectoryObject access denied; failed attempt retained.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F004','severity':'medium','title':'Overflow sentinel is not refused by every finite ceiling','finding':'The test-quality law states checked multiplication with u64::MAX fallback refuses every finite ceiling. u64::MAX is finite and a cost<=ceiling gate at that maximum admits the sentinel.','evidence':[e(24,45,50)],'recommended_action':'Return a typed overflow refusal or explicitly exclude the sentinel from valid costs/ceilings and test the boundary.','validation':'OPSKILL-CHECK-003 gives the exact finite counterexample; no claim about an uninspected runtime budget owner.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F005','severity':'medium','title':'Uncertainty is incorrectly turned into refutation','finding':'The adversarial receipt-audit rule defaults to REFUTED when uncertain. A finding not yet supported or independently decidable is UNKNOWN/UNCONFIRMED; uncertainty supplies no counterexample or refutation.','evidence':[e(37,17,25)],'recommended_action':'Use an explicit unresolved status and reserve REFUTED for a bound contradictory witness or deciding argument.','validation':'Direct full-body semantic review; no external source needed.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F006','severity':'medium','title':'Hermetic verification example does not compute the candidate hash','finding':'The command labelled verify candidate hash imports hashlib but only compares receipt fields against supplied literals. It never reads candidate bytes or test output; the companion grep cannot establish absence of cross-task evidence borrowing.','evidence':[e(45,17,33),e(45,35,53)],'recommended_action':'Provide an actual candidate-manifest rehasher and structured local execution receipt validation; label the two comparisons as partial illustration until implemented.','validation':'Full command-body inspection only; no retained command executed.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F007','severity':'low','title':'Status wording is internally inconsistent across admission surfaces','finding':'Scientific-pattern memo says IMPLEMENTED/live at the top but ends draft/not admitted with an empty sign-off. Three generated lessons say admitted by host replay yet their source admission is Unadmitted. These distinct statuses need explicit object/edition labels.','evidence':[e(22,1,7),e(22,617,644),e(43,21,23),e(43,59,62),e(47,21,23),e(47,59,62),e(52,21,23),e(52,59,62)],'recommended_action':'Name exactly what was implemented, reviewed, historically replayed and separately admitted; preserve historical claims without presenting conflicting current status.','validation':'Full-body comparison; does not infer missing historical authorizations.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F008','severity':'medium','title':'Digestion cleanup instruction omits the linked authorization condition','finding':'The main digestion skill mandates removing every completed active source, while its linked pattern allows optional cleanup only when authorized and exact custody/resolution survives. Completion of analysis alone does not make source deletion necessary or safe.','evidence':[e(41,142,152),e(42,82,89)],'recommended_action':'Make the main finish step explicitly inherit the optional authorization and custody conditions; retain no-change and unresolved cases.','validation':'Instruction consistency review only; no source removed or moved.'},
{'id':'OPSKILL-F009','severity':'medium','title':'Repeated held-out merge feedback needs a narrower validation claim','finding':'The hypothesis-tree specification calls the held-out evaluator never used for branch selection, but uses its score to decide each merge and propagates insights into subsequent trials. Repeated visible gate feedback can influence search even when only dev scores rank branches.','evidence':[e(22,279,288),e(22,338,362)],'recommended_action':'Track held-out query budget and adaptive reuse, restrict feedback, or reserve a fresh final holdout; describe the merge gate as finite nonregression evidence unless a generalization argument is provided.','validation':'Procedure-level information-flow analysis, not evidence that a particular experiment leaked.'}
]
def merge(old,new):
    d={x['id']:x for x in old};d.update({x['id']:x for x in new});return list(d.values())
r['claims']=merge(r.get('claims',[]),claims);r['findings']=merge(r.get('findings',[]),findings)
